# Directory-Specific README Guidelines

> file_patterns: ["README_*.md", "**/README_*.md"]
> description: Standards for directory-specific README documentation

## Naming Convention
> required: true

### Pattern Rules
- Use format `README_<DIRECTORY_NAME>.md`
- Directory name should be in UPPERCASE
- Use underscores for word separation
- Name should reflect directory's purpose

### Examples
- `README_TESTS.md` for test directory
- `README_DOCS.md` for documentation directory
- `README_CONFIG.md` for configuration directory
- `README_UTILS.md` for utilities directory

## Content Structure
> required: true

### Directory Overview
- Clear description of directory purpose
- Explanation of directory scope
- List of key components
- Dependencies and relationships

### File Organization
- List and explain key files
- Describe file naming conventions
- Document directory structure
- Explain any special patterns

### Component Documentation
- Document main components
- Explain component interactions
- Describe internal dependencies
- Note external dependencies

## Special Requirements

### Code Examples
- Include directory-specific examples
- Show typical usage patterns
- Demonstrate file interactions
- Provide setup instructions

### Configuration
- Document directory-specific settings
- List environment variables
- Explain configuration files
- Note default values

### Testing
- Describe test organization
- Explain test naming patterns
- Document test dependencies
- Provide test examples

## Integration Guidelines

### Parent Directory
- Explain relationship with parent
- Document inheritance patterns
- Note shared resources
- Describe communication patterns

### Sibling Directories
- Document dependencies
- Explain interactions
- Note shared resources
- Describe interfaces

### Child Directories
- List and explain subdirectories
- Document organization rules
- Explain inheritance patterns
- Note special requirements

## Maintenance

### Updates
- When to update documentation
- What to include in updates
- How to verify changes
- Update checklist

### Version Control
- Document version dependencies
- Note compatibility requirements
- Track major changes
- Maintain change history

## Validation Requirements
- Must follow naming convention
- Must document all key components
- Must explain directory purpose
- Must maintain consistency with parent README
- Must be up to date with current structure
- Must include all required sections 